35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The monitors show huge differences. One room uses four times more than another.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The other house spends forty minutes just logging readings. That’s a lot of time.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The payment log shows three late payments. People are anxious about the amounts.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The winter bills are nearly triple the summer ones. The electrician quote is steep too.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,The cooler notice stayed up all summer. People were just suffering to avoid conflict.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, if we meter, the upfront cost is high, but the fairness is clear.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, but who does the logging? I don’t want to be the one doing it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, if we use a template, it might be less manual, but still tedious.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, the late payments suggest the current system is causing stress.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,I think a fixed seasonal rate might stop the monthly arguments.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,A fixed rate means we don’t have to calculate every month.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,But what if the bill is higher than expected? Who pays the difference?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We could settle the difference once a year. That seems manageable.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I’m hesitant. The variance is too high. A fixed rate might be risky.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of settling once a year. It feels less frequent.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I’m leaning towards per-room metering. It’s the most fair, even if expensive.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’m worried about the workload. Maybe a flat share is simpler?,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,A flat share ignores the usage differences. It feels unfair to the light users.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I need to think about the winter risk. A fixed rate could be a trap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I just want peace. I think a seasonal rate might work if we agree on the numbers.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
